$DATUM 1,22-Diacetyl-1,22-diaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16,25-pentaoxoheterocycloheptacosane
(2a) Compound 2 (1.29 g, 3 mmol) was dissolved in CHCl3 (5 mL) and then
absolute pyridine (2 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 5 min, (CH3CO)2O (2 mL) added to the pale yellow
solution, and it was stirred at room temperature for 8 h. Then the
resulting solution was poured into 50 mL of light petroleum ether
(60-90°C). The lower oil phase was separated with a separatory funnel and
washed with 10 mL of light petroleum ether (60-90°C) three times.
Distilled water (20 mL) was added to the oil, extracted with
dichloromethane (2 x 10 mL). The organic layer was dried over anhydrous
MgSO4, the solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue
was dried in vacuum-drying oven at room temperature to yield the pale
yellow viscous oil, 1.11 g (yield 72%);
1,22-Diacetyl-1,22-diaza-3,6:17,20-dibenzo-7,10,13,16,25-pentaoxoheterocycloheptacosane
(2a), 1.11 g (yield 72%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.14 (6H, m,
-CH3), δ = 3.05-3.19 (4H, m, N-CH2-C-O), δ = 3.68-3.79 (4H, m, O-CH2C-N),
δ = 3.97 (4H, m, O-CH2-C-O-C), δ = 4.07 (4H, m, Ar-O-C-CH2O), δ = 4.14
(4H, m, Ar-OCH2), δ =4.31-4.53 (4H, d, N-CH2Ar), δ =6.71-7.27 (8H, m,
Ar-H). IR (KBr/cm-1): 3449, 2928, 2869, 1635, 1609, 1512, 1448, 1418,
1361, 1299, 1247, 1124, 1066, 1038, 933, 822; MS (FAB) m/z: 515[M + 1]+;
anal. ca1cd. for C28H38N2O7: C, 65.37; N, 5.45; H, 7.39; found: C, 65.25;
N, 5.58; H, 6.94.
