$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. A solution of amine 1a-d (0.020 mol) and
maleic anhydride (2.24 g, 0.023 mol) in benzene (100 ml) was heated at
reflux for 10 h to give pure carboxylic acids 2a.
(3aS*,6S*,7R*,7aR*)-2-(2-Furylmethyl)-6-iodo-1-oxo-1,2,3,6,7,7a-hexahydro-3a,6-epoxyisoindole-7-carboxylic
Acid (2dB); Colorless crystals, yield 70%. Empirical formula: C14H12INO5;
Found, %: C, 42.13; H, 2.67; N, 3.15; Calculated, %: C, 41.92; H, 3.02;
N, 3.49; Mp: >205°CС (decomp.); IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1670 (NCO), 1745
(СО2Н); 1Н NMR spectrum, δ, ppm (J, Hz): 2.88 (1Н, d, J = 8.8, Н); 2.93
(1Н, d, J = 8.8, Н; 3.62 (1Н, d, J = 11.8) and 3.92 (1Н, d, J = 11.8,
3-CН2); 4.30 (1Н, d, J = 16.0) and 4.50 (1Н, d, J = 16.0, 2-CH2); 6.35
(1Н, dd, J = 0.8, J = 3.2, Н); 6.41 (1Н, dd, J = 1.8, J = 3.2, Н); 6.54
(1Н, d, J = 5.6, Н; 6.55 (1Н, d, J = 5.6, Н; 7.58 (1Н, dd, J = 0.8, J =
1.8, Н); 13C NMR, δ, ppm: 38.8 (СH2); 47.3 (C-3); 52.0 (Са); 52.8 (C-7);
87.9 (C-3a); 88.3 (C-6); 108.0 (C-4'); 110.5 (C-3'); 135.5 (C-5); 137.2
(C-4); 142.7 (C-5'); 149.8 (C-2'); 169.3 (C-1); 170.4 (CO2H); MS m/z
(Irel, %): 401 [М]+ (6), 320 (64), 276 (14), 222 (46), 207 (72), 194
(67), 179 (39), 147 (16), 128 (67), 109 (38), 96 (73), 80 (100), 59 (54),
53 (85), 44 (49).
